pr: n10
title: JVM unit artifact: QAST-only compiler, stage0 as unit artifacts, the class road deleted (milestone 4)
branch: pr/10-unit-artifact-m4

# Section N15 of the survey plus the five post-survey commits (log lines 359..372, 14 commits).
# Every deletion stays a commit of its own; only two obvious pairs are folded.
# Hazard H1: 9844a0de9 (stage0 regenerated as unit artifacts) must follow 5cf759de6 (JASTNodes
# gone) -- it does, and no other stage0 commit is in this PR.

= keep
- c6af33aa3 unit compiler: a QAST-only driver hands the writer a unit record -- no JAST tree, no operand stack, no per-block stub; the registries stay as data

= keep
- 5cf759de6 unit compiler: the JASTNodes module and nqp's JAST op closures are gone; nine stage targets

= keep
- 9844a0de9 stage0: regenerated as unit artifacts from the JAST-free compiler; stage compiles enter through UnitMain

= keep
- 1a658daa1 runtime: the class road's writer and loaders are gone -- jast2bc, compilejast, loadcompunit's define branch, the sidecar reader, setLexValues, enterFromMain, IndyBootstrap; BytecodeVersion moves to runtime/

= keep
- 4b261b3b2 runtime: the loader is Kotlin and knows one road -- LibraryLoader.java and its four class loaders are gone; UnitLoader loads, primes and reads

= keep
- 14df06863 interop: adaptor classes are plain classes; AdaptorUnit builds their code refs from bound method handles; the reflective code-ref road and CodeRefAnnotation are gone

= keep
- d8116d7c9 runtime: a torn frame runs its exit handler with the result absent, then gives back its count (LEAVE on exceptional exit)

= keep
- 929f73b11 engine: a suspended fused op resumes through its finisher -- the op's tail runs on the inner call's value instead of taking that value as the op's result

= keep
- e270f070d encoder: patch_params keeps the parameter prologue's deferred code-ref slots -- a BVal in a param default or where constraint no longer resolves to the mainline (qbid 0); NQP_DO_TRACE shows $!do binds

= keep
- d24431b68 docs: the class road is gone -- BytecodeVersion moved, ASM stays for P6Opaque and the adaptors

= runtime: a suspended frame keeps its exit handler and its live count
# moved: b3d75f993 (CallFrame.kt only) pulled ahead of 47697ca29 (Compiler.nqp,
# RxDescriptor.nqp, TruffleEncoder.nqp) and 3b9615f4b (t/jvm/16-op-registry.t) -- disjoint; it
# corrects what the first commit's leaveSuspended did, so the pair is one change.
CallFrame separates its two one-shots: the live-invocation count and the exit handler. A save
into a continuation (leaveSuspended) restores tc.curFrame and nothing else -- the frame is still
live, so a second invocation of the same static frame (SEQUENCE building a range with SEQUENCE)
resolves its outer correctly; the real exit, leave() or leaveTorn(), gives the count back once and
runs the handler once, so a LEAVE in a gather fires at its exit and not at the first take.
UnitLoader marks a unit loaded only after it loaded; NqpOps.bindattr traces once per bind.
- 908134f3f runtime: a continuation-captured frame keeps its exit handler for its real exit; UnitLoader marks a unit loaded only after it loaded
- b3d75f993 runtime: a suspended frame is still live -- the save road keeps its invocation count, so a second invocation of the same static frame resolves its outer correctly

= compiler: is_inlinable from the classlib registry and the encoder's rows
add_core_op's :$inlinable default seeded %core_inlinability for the 44 hand-mapped core ops; the
class road's deletion took those closures and left is_inlinable answering 0 for add_i, if, while,
bind, callmethod and the rest, so RakuAST inlined no routine containing one and the CORE setting
was built with routine inlining and native lowering off. The default now derives from the encoder's
rows as core_op_supported does, with %core_noninlinable naming the twelve ops that carried
:!inlinable; the classlib rows still win. t/jvm/16-op-registry pins inlinability and supports-op.
- 47697ca29 compiler: is_inlinable answers from the classlib registry, the encoder's rows and an explicit non-inlinable table -- the deleted add_core_op closures were the table's source
- 3b9615f4b tests: the op registry (inlinability, supports-op)

= keep
- 108fa2936 runtime: a unit stays loaded when a continuation capture crosses its load block
